        <p class="p4" style="margin-top:63.6pt">PRIVACY POLICY</p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">ACCEPTANCE OF TERMS</p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          This privacy policy governs the manner in which Mysa Innovations Private Limited including
          its affiliates and subsidiaries (“<span style="font-weight:bold">Company</span>”)
          collects, uses, maintains and discloses information collected from users (each, a “<span
            style="font-weight:bold">User</span
          >”) of the name <a href="https://www.mysa.io" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
            ><span style="color:#1155cc;text-decoration:underline">www.mysa.io</span></a
          > website and services offered by the Company (“<span style="font-weight:bold"
            >Website</span
          >”). This privacy policy applies to the Website and all services offered by the Company.
          You agree to and are bound by the terms and conditions set forth below and in any modified
          or additional terms that the Company may publish from time to time (collectively, the “<span
            style="font-weight:bold">Privacy Policy</span
          >”).
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          If the User does not agree to all of the terms and conditions contained in the Terms of
          Use and this Privacy Policy, do not access or use this Website.
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          PERSONAL<span style="font-weight:normal"> </span>INFORMATION
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The personal information collected, received, processed, stored, dealt or handled by the
          Company includes, [name, contact details, location, unique identifiers, email address].
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company may collect personal information from Users in a variety of ways, including,
          but not limited to, when Users visit the Website, registers on the Website,  seeks
          information in connection with other activities, services, features or resources the
          Company makes available on the Website. Users may be asked for, as appropriate, name,
          email address, mailing address, phone number.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company will collect personal identification information from Users only if they
          voluntarily submit such information to the Company. Users can always refuse to supply
          personal information, except that it may prevent them from engaging in certain Website
          related activities.
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          NON<span style="font-weight:normal">-</span>PERSONAL<span style="font-weight:normal">
          </span>INFORMATION
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company may collect non-personal information about Users whenever they interact with
          the Website. Non-personal information may include the browser name, the type of computer
          and technical information about Users means of connection to the Website, such as the
          operating system and the internet service providers utilized and other similar
          information.
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">USE OF THE INFORMATION COLLECTED</p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company uses the User’s personal information for the following purposes:
        </p>
        <p class="p7">
          to identify the User once it registers on the Website;<br />to create the User login and
          administer the User accounts;<br />to contact the User and respond to User questions or
          requests;<br />to send the User communication regarding the services and products;<br />to
          provide access to desirable content and products based on the User’s preferences;<br />to
          provide better usability, troubleshooting and site maintenance;<br />to understand which
          parts of the Website are visited and how frequently;<br />to screen the orders for
          potential risks or fraud; and<br />to improve and optimize the Website (for example, by
          generating analytics about how the User’s browse and interact with the Website, and to
          assess the success of the Company’s marketing and advertising campaigns).
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:25.3pt">SHARING OF USER’S PERSONAL INFORMATION</p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company may share the User information with these third parties for those limited
          purposes provided that the User have given the Company permission. If the User access
          those links, the User will leave the Website. The Company does not control those sites or
          their privacy practices, which may differ from the Company. The Company does not endorse
          or make any representations about third-party sites.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company is not responsible for examining or evaluating, and does not warrant the
          offerings of, any businesses or individuals or the content of their website. The Company
          does not assume any responsibility or liability for the actions, products, services, and
          content of any other third parties. User should carefully review the legal statements and
          other conditions of use of any website which the User accesses through a link from this
          Website. The User linking to any other off-site websites is at the User’s own risk.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company never collects or maintains information at the Website from those the Company
          knows are under the age of 18 (eighteen) years. No part of the Website is structured to
          attract anyone under the age of 18 (eighteen) years.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company may use third-party service providers to help the Company operate its business
          and the Website or administer activities on the Company’s behalf, such as sending out
          newsletters or surveys.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          <span style="font-weight:bold">IDENTITY THEFT</span>
          <br />There may be instances when the User receive a seemingly legitimate looking e-mail
          asking the User personal information from the User such as the User’s credit card details,
          bank account details, one-time passwords, contact information, etc. The Company will never
          ask for such information from you via e-mail.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          Such activities are usually carried on by unauthorized individuals and are illegal in
          nature. They are called phishing or identity theft. In case of any suspicion of such
          activity or on receiving such an e-mail the User should be certain it was not sent by the
          Company. The Company advises the User to not respond to such mail and to take whatever
          action you see fit.
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">WEB BROWSER COOKIES</p>
        <p class="p6">
          A cookie is an element of data that a website can send to the User’s browser, which may
          then store it on the User’s system. The Company uses cookies in some of its pages to store
          visitors' preferences and record session information. The information that the Company
          collects is then used to ensure a more personalised service level for the Users.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The User can adjust the settings on its browser so that the User will be notified when it
          receives a cookie, or to disable the cookies associated with the Website. The User should
          refer to its browser documentation to check if cookies have been enabled on the User’s
          computer or to request not to receive cookies.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Website may use “cookies” to enhance User experience. User's web browser places
          cookies on their hard drive for record-keeping purposes and sometimes to track information
          about them. User may choose to set their web browser to refuse cookies or to alert the
          User when cookies are being sent. If they do so, note that some parts of the Website may
          not function properly.
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">DATA RETENTION</p>
        <p class="p6">
          The Company will retain the User information only for as long as is necessary for the
          purposes set out in this policy. The Company will retain and use the User’s information to
          the extent necessary to comply with the Company’s legal obligations (for example, if the
          Company is required to retain the User’s data to comply with applicable laws), resolve
          disputes, and enforce the Company’s legal agreements and policies.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          The Company encourages the User to review the information and inform about any
          discrepancies and information found to be inaccurate shall be corrected or amended. Please
          reach out to the Company at mail@mysa.io in case the User would like to review the
          information collected by the Company. The User shall at all times, take adequate necessary
          precautions, at the User’s end, to preserve the integrity and security of the User’s data
          which shall include and not be limited to the User personal information. All information
          disclosed by the User shall be deemed to be disclosed willingly and without any coercion.
        </p>
        <p class="p5" style="margin-top:12.6pt">LOG DATA</p>
        <p class="p6">
          The Company want to inform the User that whenever you use the Website or avail the
          services, the Company collects data from the User device called log data (“<span
            style="font-weight:bold">Log Data</span
          >”). This Log Data may include information such as the User device’s internet protocol (“<span
            style="font-weight:bold">IP</span
          >”) address, device name, operating system version, configuration of the app when
          utilising the Website services, the time and date of the User’s use of the Website
          service, and other statistics for the purposes of audit trials, trouble shooting, and
          other purposes.
        </p>
        <p class="p6" style="margin-top:12.6pt">
          <span style="font-weight:bold">INFORMATION SECURITY</span>
          <br />The Company works to protect the User’s information from loss, misuse or
          unauthorized alteration by using industry-recognized security safeguards, coupled with
          carefully developed security procedures and practices. The Company maintains electronic
          and procedural safeguards of all information. The Company uses both internal and external
          resources to review the Company’s security procedures. The security practices and
          procedures contains managerial, technical, operational and physical security control
          measures that are commensurate with the personal information being collected, received,
          processed, stored, dealt or handled and the nature of the business of the Company.
        </p>
        <p class="p8" style="margin-top:28.3pt">SEND TO MYSA CHROME EXTENSION</p>
        <p class="p9">
          “Send to Mysa” is a Chrome extension published by the Company. It runs inside a User’s own
          Gmail account in the Chrome browser and lets the User forward invoices and receipts to the
          Company’s ingestion addresses (for example, <span style="color:#1264a3"
            >yourcompany@invoice.mysa.io</span
          >), and see the status of bills and reimbursements they have submitted. This section
          explains how the extension accesses, uses, shares, stores, protects, retains and deletes
          Google user data. Where this section differs from any other part of this policy, this
          section applies to Google user data.
        </p>
        <p class="p8" style="margin-top:21.6pt">1. Data Accessed</p>
        <p class="p9">With the User’s permission, the extension accesses:</p>
        <p class="p10">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>The Gmail page the User has open: to show
          the Send to Mysa button and identify which email(s) the User has selected, including the
          sender’s name and email address and Gmail message and thread identifiers.
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>Read Gmail: to read the emails the User
          chooses to send to Mysa, including their attachments, sender, subject and date; to read
          status-update emails and upload-result files sent by the Company (from<a
            href="https://www.mysa.io"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
          </a><a href="https://www.mysa.io" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
            ><span style="color:#1264a3">mysa.io</span></a
          > and mysa.one addresses), including when they appear in an email thread the User has opened;
          and, only for senders the User has turned on for auto-send, to check for new emails with attachments
          from those senders.
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>Send email as the User: to forward the
          selected email or its attachments to the Mysa ingestion address the User has configured.
        </p>
        <p class="p12">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>Chrome identity: only to obtain the sign-in
          token Chrome issues for the two Gmail permissions above.
        </p>
        <p class="p9">
          The extension does not access the User’s contacts, calendar, Drive or any other Google
          data.
        </p>
        <p class="p8" style="margin-top:21.6pt">2. Data Usage</p>
        <p class="p9">
          Google user data is used only to provide features the User can see and control:
        </p>
        <p class="p10">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>forwarding the emails or attachments the
          User selects to the User’s Mysa ingestion address, and merging attachments into a single
          PDF when the User asks;
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>where the User has turned on auto-send for
          a specific sender, checking once an hour for new emails with attachments from that sender
          and forwarding them; auto-send can be turned off or deleted for any sender at any time;
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>warning the User before they send a
          document they appear to have sent before;
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>showing the status of submitted bills and
          reimbursements, read from the Company’s own status emails in the User’s mailbox; and
        </p>
        <p class="p12">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>showing the results of bulk uploads, read
          from the result files the Company emails back.
        </p>
        <p class="p9">
          Google user data is not used for advertising, is not sold, is not used to build user
          profiles, and is not used to train artificial intelligence or machine-learning models. The
          Company does not access the User’s mailbox; it receives only the emails that are forwarded
          to it, either by the User directly or through auto-send for senders the User has turned
          on.
        </p>
        <p class="p8" style="margin-top:21.6pt">3. Data Sharing</p>
        <p class="p9">
          The extension sends Google user data to one place only: the Mysa ingestion addresses the
          User has configured, as an ordinary email sent from the User’s own Gmail account, exactly
          as if the User had forwarded it by hand. Those documents then become part of the User’s
          Mysa account and are handled under the rest of this policy. Apart from that, Google user
          data is not shared with, sold to or transferred to any third party. The extension contains
          no analytics, advertising or other third-party code. The general statements about sharing
          information with third parties elsewhere in this policy do not apply to Google user data.
        </p>
        <p class="p8" style="margin-top:21.6pt">4. Data Storage &amp; Protection</p>
        <p class="p9">
          The extension has no server of its own and makes no call to any Company system. Gmail data
          is processed only inside the User’s browser and travels only between the browser and
          Google’s Gmail API over encrypted (HTTPS) connections. Sign-in tokens are issued and held
          by Chrome’s built-in Google sign-in; the extension does not store them itself.
        </p>
        <p class="p9">The extension keeps a small amount of data in Chrome’s extension storage:</p>
        <p class="p10">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>the Mysa tenant(s) the User has set up, and
          the User’s remembered choice for each sender (the sender’s email address, document type,
          whether to merge attachments and which tenant to use). These use Chrome sync, so they
          follow the User’s own Google account when Chrome sync is turned on;
        </p>
        <p class="p12">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>a log of documents sent (each email’s
          sender name and address, subject line, Gmail message and thread identifiers, and file
          names, sizes and digital fingerprints), a list of recent automatic sends, and the User’s
          auto-send settings (each sender’s name, document type, optional subject filter and recent
          send times). These are used only to detect duplicates, run auto-send and show the User
          their history, and they stay in that browser only.
        </p>
        <p class="p9">None of this data is sent to or stored on Company servers.</p>
        <p class="p8" style="margin-top:21.6pt">5. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</p>
        <p class="p9">
          The send log keeps only the most recent 2,000 entries, the list of automatic sends keeps
          the most recent 50, and each auto-send setting keeps its 40 most recent send times; older
          entries are deleted automatically. Other settings are kept until the User changes or
          removes them. The User can:
        </p>
        <p class="p10">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>remove remembered senders, tenants and
          auto-send settings from within the extension;
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>delete the data the extension stores in
          their browser by removing the extension from Chrome;
        </p>
        <p class="p11">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>clear data held through Chrome sync from
          their Chrome sync settings; and
        </p>
        <p class="p12">
          <span class="d-bul" style="width:18pt">●</span>revoke the extension’s access to their
          Google account at any time at https://myaccount.google.com/permissions.
        </p>
        <p class="p9">
          For help, or to request deletion of documents already forwarded to Mysa, the User can
          contact <span style="color:#1264a3">support@mysa.io</span>. Such requests are handled
          under the deletion procedure in this policy.
        </p>
        <p class="p9">Limited Use</p>
        <p class="p9">
          Send to Mysa’s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs
          will adhere to the<a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
          </a><a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
            ><span style="color:#1264a3">Google API Services User Data Policy</span></a
          >, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>
